WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.720
Qatar is the wealthiest country on the planet.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:16.260
Their citizens enjoy a higher GDP per capita
than the Swiss, or indeed any of the nationals

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.270
from any of the other oil-rich monarchies.

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:21.840
But today we are not going to talk about this.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:26.580
In fact, the most important fact of this country
is not their wealth, nor their absolute monarchy,

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:31.110
or their ties with radical terrorist groups.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:42.079
Beyond any doubt, what made this country famous
can be summarized in just two words: AL JAZEERA.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:48.560
It is the most influential TV network in the
Arab World and one of the most important news

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:50.360
networks on the entire planet.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:55.111
At the beginning of the 90s, the Royal Family
that rules Qatar with an iron fist, the AL

00:00:55.111 --> 00:00:57.399
THANI house, had a dream.

00:00:57.399 --> 00:01:01.129
They wanted to turn their nation into the
hegemonic leader in the region.

00:01:01.129 --> 00:01:04.670
But the question was: How could they achieve
this?

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:11.390
We are talking about a tiny country, with
a smaller population than the city of Chicago.

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:15.250
Of course they couldn't rival Saudi Arabia
in the military field, and sharia law made

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.850
it impossible to be a financial powerhouse.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:21.420
Further, their geographical position was nothing
special either...

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:27.790
There was only one possible strategy and that
was the idea of so-called "soft power".

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:33.720
In other words: influence, diplomacy and 
"well" propaganda!

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:38.390
Since then, Qatar has invested more than any
other country in improving their image to

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:44.620
outsiders by doing things like hosting the
Soccer World Cup in 2022, a Formula 1 race,

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:48.910
and even directly sponsoring soccer teams.

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:56.509
But, among all these projects, the most successful
and famous of them all has to be their TV

00:01:56.509 --> 00:01:58.140
network: AL JAZEERA.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:02.340
They are the market leader, in terms of audience,
in the entire arab world.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:07.369
In fact their market share surpasses all of
their rivals put together!

00:02:07.369 --> 00:02:22.400
And this is all despite the fact that the
channel is banned in most countries.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:26.900
Al Jazeera has lead to the overthrow of governments
in several nations, they have amplified the

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:31.629
effect of the arab spring and they've even
become the unofficial loudspeaker for some

00:02:31.629 --> 00:02:33.060
terrorist groups...

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:37.450
Since the attacks of the September 11th, Al
Jazeera has become, in many ways, the only

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:42.879
source of information for understanding what
is going on in some parts of the world.

00:02:42.879 --> 00:02:44.900
Even CNN buys their footage...

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:48.099
In other words: they are a respected media
institution.

00:02:48.099 --> 00:02:53.760
But, then again, you might wonder: isn't
Al Jazeera just a state propaganda channel?

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:58.129
I mean to what extent should we really trust
their information?

00:02:58.129 --> 00:02:59.800
What's their ideology?

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:03.569
Well, today we are going to answer all these
questions.

00:03:03.569 --> 00:03:07.690
But before we do that, let's take a look
at some history.

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:10.840
THE IMPORTANCE OF BEING UNIQUE

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:16.090
In 1995, the BBC closed their arab channel
because the Saudi Government wanted to interfere

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.910
in their editorial process.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:20.430
150 journalists got fired.

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:24.900
All of them were Arab journalists, who were
trained at one of the most prestigious media

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:26.960
organisations in the world.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:31.090
These people had a deep knowledge of Muslim
culture but, at the same time, they couldn�t

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:33.510
meet the high standards of Western media.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:37.200
This is where the, the Emir of Qatar at the
time, HAMAD AL THANI, comes in.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:47.549
Al Thani had just come to power and had a
clear vision for his country: he wanted to

00:03:47.549 --> 00:03:50.340
become the leader of the Islamic world.

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:55.299
In order to achieve that, those 150 unemployed
journalists were given an opportunity...

00:03:55.299 --> 00:03:59.520
As soon as they lost their jobs, Qatar offered
them a brand new one.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:00.520
Their mission?

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:03.480
To create a new news network.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:07.070
An Arabic-speaking TV network that would meet
the quality of Western media...

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:08.560
At any cost.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:12.739
Qatar's government gave them a $147 million
loan.

00:04:12.739 --> 00:04:19.690
With that, this team of 150 journalists could
buy state of the art studios, have correspondents

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:27.190
in many countries and broadcast through a
satellite.

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:31.500
Every little detail was taken care of. For
example to design the logo, the Emir made

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:32.650
a public contest.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:37.130
Finally, this one, that you see on the screen
now, was the winner and, as you can see it

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:41.680
reads "AL JAZEERA" in Arabic.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:48.180
Finally, in 1996, Al Jazeera, that means "the
island" in arabic, started broadcasting

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.490
to the Arab world.

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:53.110
In very little time, they surpassed the rest
of their rivals...

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:57.080
Think about it: back in the day, Arab TV was
extremely boring.

00:04:57.080 --> 00:05:02.430
In this part of the world, freedom of expression
doesn't really exist, and therefore TV news

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:04.440
just offered official announcements.

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:05.940
Al Jazeera was different.

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:10.250
They had no problems in criticizing various
politicians and royal families.

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:14.780
They showed corruption scandals and they even
interviewed political dissidents.

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:19.639
All of this with a unique, dynamic style,
that had never been seen on an Arabic speaking

00:05:19.639 --> 00:05:22.040
TV station.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:26.360
Nevertheless, the real turning point for Al
Jazeera was on 9-11...

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:30.940
OSAMA BIN LADEN used this TV network to broadcast
his claim to the terrorist attack.

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:36.509
All of a sudden, the name "Al Jazeera"
was being said on TV news across the world.

00:05:36.509 --> 00:05:37.560
But not only that!

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:42.130
A month after the terrorist attack, the American
government declared war to Afghanistan.

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:47.479
Back then, all the big media corporations
like CNN or CNBC had correspondents in Tokyo,

00:05:47.479 --> 00:05:51.570
London or Berlin, but no one had thought Kabul
would be that newsworthy...

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:58.580
And, well, guess who DID have an office in
the Afghan capital?

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:01.360
Yep, that would be Al Jazeera.

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:05.020
Since they were a channel targeted to the
muslim World, they had correspondents in all

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:06.449
of the Muslim countries.

00:06:06.449 --> 00:06:10.650
Suddenly, Al Jazeera footage was appearing
on televisions all around the world.

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:16.110
This is why, in 2004, the Emir of Qatar realized
that what he had was not only a powerful tool

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:20.270
to reach the Arab world, but indeed the world
at large.

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:24.810
And this is how English Al Jazeera was born,
and it was ready to broadcast into the most

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:32.530
competitive media market in the world: The
United States of America.

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:36.970
Since then, Al Jazeera has become the TV news
that talks about countries that never appear

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:38.669
on American TV news.

00:06:38.669 --> 00:06:39.669
Want to know about Africa?

00:06:39.669 --> 00:06:40.840
Tune into Al Jazeera!

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:41.840
Middle East?

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:43.520
Go to Al Jazeera!

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:44.520
Central Asia?

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:45.979
Yeah, you get the idea...

00:06:45.979 --> 00:06:51.330
But wait a minute because things are not as
great as they seem to be!

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:57.940
Don't forget we are talking about a TV network
being paid by a government to influence other

00:06:57.940 --> 00:06:59.460
countries!

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:02.610
Starting to sound a bit like it might be propaganda
right?

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:06.410
Well, let's see:

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:10.220
ISLAM'S ENFANT TERRIBLE

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:15.050
As we said before, Al Jazeera was the first
Arab TV network that openly criticized the

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:18.620
governments of other countries.

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:24.940
And, rather unsurprisingly, this was not always
welcome.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:28.080
Especially given that most of these other
countries are dictatorships.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:34.380
So, in 2011, an uprising in Tunisia started,
and the dictator of this nation abandoned

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:35.380
it.

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:37.830
All of these facts could have had little to
no impact abroad.

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:43.400
But Al Jazeera had deep coverage of this uprising
so that it could be seen in other countries.

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:48.449
Since it was a satellite station, their signal
was arriving to sets all across North Africa

00:07:48.449 --> 00:07:54.480
and the Arab Peninsula.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:58.940
This is how the inhabitants of other countries
next to Tunisia like Egypt, saw their neighbours

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:03.020
protesting and thought: Wait a minute...
we also have a dictator, couldn't we do

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:07.650
something similar? And, of course, every
person in opposition to HOSNI MUBARAK, had

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:12.270
a news show that they could watch? And,
of course, this was not something that went

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:18.160
over brilliantly with those dictators!

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:22.560
Al Jazeera shut down in Egypt as Mubarak fights
for control of airwaves

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:27.860
But, what exactly is the problem here?

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:31.270
Well, censoring a satellite TV station is
harder than it seems.

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:33.919
Of course, you can forbid it if you want.

00:08:33.919 --> 00:08:38.870
But if someone wants to access the station
and have a satellite dish, then technically

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:47.500
it's possible.

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:52.630
So in a matter of months, all these Arab citizens
were seeing their neighbouring countries overthrowing

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:53.970
their dictators.

00:08:53.970 --> 00:09:01.519
And this explains, in part, the Arab Spring
phenomenon.

00:09:01.519 --> 00:09:04.830
But wait a minute because not everything is
so perfect!

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:09.260
Of course, Al Jazeera helped to finish off
a lot of dictatorships, but the truth is the

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:15.380
people they promoted on their network were
not really any more democratic

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:23.600
For years, the Muslim Brotherhood's spiritual
leader, was given his own television show

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:29.010
on Al Jazeera.

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:33.800
Even DAESH, the Islamic State, was portrayed
by Al Jazeera as just an "opposition force"

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:38.180
to AL-ASSAD in Syria or even as a group of
"moderate rebels".

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:42.610
The same happened with other Sunni radical
terrorists like AL QAEDA.

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:47.410
And now you might wonder: Is AL JAZEERA
a network that stands for radicalism and against

00:09:47.410 --> 00:09:48.410
the West?

00:09:48.410 --> 00:09:51.740
Well, the truth is they've been also accused
of the opposite...

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:55.760
Just ask the Emir of Bahrain and his government?

00:09:55.760 --> 00:10:01.160
Minister of Information Nabil al-Hamr told
journalists that Al-Jazeera's correspondents

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:03.260
had been barred from Bahrain.

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:07.570
Al-Hamr claimed that the station was
a medium for "Zionist infiltration in the

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:08.570
Gulf region."

00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:11.000
Surprised?

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:18.990
Well, for many, Al Jazeera is Zionist, Western
propaganda, for others, it is the TV station

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:19.990
of the radicals...

00:10:19.990 --> 00:10:25.140
In fact, the only common ground for Al Jazeera
when it comes to ideology is the interests

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:30.700
of the ones who finances them: the royal house
of AL THANI who, by the way, don't support

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:37.220
freedom of speech on their own country.

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:43.530
WikiLeaks cables claim al-Jazeera changed
coverage to suit Qatari foreign policy

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:47.150
Nevertheless, this doesn't mean they cannot
show the dark side of Qatar.

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:51.980
In fact, despite being paid by a Royal House,
Al Jazeera is more independent than many other

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:57.570
state-sponsored news networks.

00:10:57.570 --> 00:11:02.580
For instance, what you see on the screen are
extracts from a talk show about the near-slave-like

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:09.000
working conditions suffered by the immigrants
who work in Qatar as construction workers.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:13.321
In this show, foreign trade unionists were
invited and had the chance to openly criticize

00:11:13.321 --> 00:11:15.820
the AL THANI family and their policies.

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:20.560
In other words, Al Jazeera's directors are
smart enough to limit their propaganda and

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:22.570
not lose their audience.

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:27.250
Of course, they have an ideology and a lot
of interests to meet, but they are all aware

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:32.620
that, in today's world you can't silence the
reality of what is happening - if you don't

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:36.240
tell it, others will tell it for you.

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:42.010
At the end of the day, Al Jazeera itself is
forbidden in almost all countries in the region

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:43.660
- including Saudi Arabia.

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:48.649
Nonetheless, they are still the most influential
and most watched TV network.

00:11:48.649 --> 00:11:52.520
Everyone knows who pays for them, but, at
the same time, they are the only source for

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:54.089
many news topics.

00:11:54.089 --> 00:11:57.040
In fact, the Al Jazeera model has lots of
copycats.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:00.579
In 2003, the Saudis founded their own channel,
Al Arabiya.

00:12:00.579 --> 00:12:10.050
Further the American Government has their
own Arabic-speaking network, called AH HURRA.

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:14.810
And what about the Iranian TV?

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:19.320
Hispan TV is a Spanish-speaking network paid
for by the Iranian government in order to

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:21.019
influence in the Hispanic world.

00:12:21.019 --> 00:12:24.870
They also have an English-speaking channel
called Press TV.

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:30.420
In 2005, Russia launched Russia Today, also
known as RT.

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:34.060
Meanwhile, Al Jazeera keeps exploring new
possibilities...

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:43.020
Their latest creation is A+J, a Facebook page
where they share viral news.

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:52.110
So now our question for you is: Would you
stop watching Al Jazeera because you think

00:12:52.110 --> 00:12:53.110
it's propaganda?

00:12:53.110 --> 00:12:57.130
Or you will keep enjoying their shows while
adding a pinch of salt?

00:12:57.130 --> 00:13:00.990
